<issue>
The following bug was reported (this is the only specification you are given):
Title: concurrent calls to `.clear()` and the ingestion API causes crash and corruption (fjall, a Rust LSM-tree storage engine)
Body: Running this program eventually crashes and corrupts the database:

```rust
let db = fjall::Database::builder("./db").max_journaling_size(67108864).manual_journal_persist(true).open()?;
std::thread::scope(|spawner| {
    let keyspace = db.keyspace("keyspace1", fjall::KeyspaceCreateOptions::default).unwrap();
    spawner.spawn({ let keyspace = keyspace.clone(); move || {
        for _ in 0..1000 { keyspace.clear()?; std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(10)); } Ok(()) }});
    spawner.spawn({ let keyspace = keyspace.clone(); move || {
        for _ in 0..1000 { let mut igst = keyspace.start_ingestion()?;
            for i in 0..=10240 { igst.write(format!("key{i:09}"), [(i%256) as u8; 256])?; } igst.finish()?; } Ok(()) }});
});
```

It eventually panics in a worker thread with `assertion left == right failed: invalid table IDs` (lsm-tree version management), poisons a lock, and the process hangs. The database is left corrupted, leaking thousands of versions under db/keyspaces/. The crash happens faster with manual_journal_persist(true). One thread clears the keyspace repeatedly while another ingests; they are not safely synchronized.

</issue>

