## Overview

You're a software engineer interacting continuously with a computer by submitting shell commands. You'll be helping fix the bug described in the issue above. Your task is specifically to make changes to non-test source files in order to fix the issue in a way that is general and consistent with the codebase.

This is an interactive process: you think and issue commands, see the result, then think and issue your next command(s).

## The shell

The repository lives only on a remote box. You reach it ONLY through the proxy `/tmp/box-sh`, e.g. `/tmp/box-sh-min 'ls && sed -n "1,40p" src/keyspace/mod.rs'`. The proxy lands you in the repository root. Every command runs in a fresh subshell (directory and environment changes do NOT persist between commands; prefix with `cd ... && ...` within a single command if needed). Do not use your own local filesystem; it is an unrelated scratch dir.

## Boundaries

